<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="090" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Project wrap-up</title>
    <phase>9 Wrap-up</phase>
    <gate>all tasks complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Project close with a mandatory test-diet gate.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Documentation and archival with one mandatory skill invocation.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>medium</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Project close; runs once, last.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>all</deps>
    <tags>documentation,wrapup</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Close the project: run the test diet, verify every success criterion, write lessons-learned, and set the README to Complete.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer.</role>
  <goal>The project is closed with every success criterion verified or explicitly deferred with an Issue URL.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>CLAUDE.md section 7 makes /test-diet a BINDING gate on a wrap-up task: it reconciles tests added during the project against the build-versus-maintain classifier. The skill is read-only and emits commands for a reviewer.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/README.md</file>
      <file role="new">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/lessons-learned.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: /test-diet is MANDATORY before marking the project complete (CLAUDE.md section 7). Skipping it is a HARD WARNING and the wrap-up PR must cite the report or document the skip rationale.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: verify each of the eleven success criteria individually. For criterion 2, state explicitly whether it passed on SEEDED data or on data nobody authored to make it pass. Those are different readings of it works and the risk is only retired by the second.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: anything incomplete gets a GitHub Issue URL in notes/defer-issues.md. Nothing is merely listed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: run scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 and resolve any disagreement before closing.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Project close</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/test-diet/SKILL.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above before touching code.</step>
    <step order="1">Invoke /test-diet and record the report at notes/test-diet-report.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Walk the eleven success criteria and record pass, fail or deferred for each, with evidence.</step>
    <step order="3">For criterion 2, state plainly whether it passed on seeded or unseeded data.</step>
    <step order="4">For criterion 11, cite the measured recall figure and the set size.</step>
    <step order="5">Run scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 and resolve any disagreement.</step>
    <step order="6">Write notes/lessons-learned.md, including what the four /design-to-spec decisions (D-9 to D-12) cost to discover late.</step>
    <step order="7">File GitHub Issues for anything incomplete and record the URLs.</step>
    <step order="8">Set README status to Complete and reset current-task.md to none.</step>
    <step order="9">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="10">Record any deviation from this POML in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any success criterion cannot be verified, STOP and escalate rather than marking the project complete with an unverified criterion. Criteria 2, 10 and 11 can each fail the project, and reporting one as passed when it was not is the failure mode the honesty rules exist to prevent.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No lessons-learned or test-diet report exists for this project; both are required close-out artifacts named by CLAUDE.md section 7 and the task-create wrap-up rule.</existing>
    <extension>No file to extend: these are per-project artifacts created once at close. Note that this is DOCUMENT surface, not a code component, so the section 11 three-question gate is answered here for completeness rather than because a component is being introduced.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without lessons-learned the next project repeats this one discoveries, and without the test-diet report the project closes with scaffolding-class tests left in the maintained suite, which CLAUDE.md section 7 makes a hard warning.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/lessons-learned.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/test-diet-report.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/README.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given /test-diet, when run, then notes/test-diet-report.md exists and the wrap-up PR cites it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the eleven success criteria, when reviewed, then each has a recorded pass, fail or deferred verdict with evidence.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given criterion 2, when reported, then it states explicitly whether it passed on seeded or unseeded data.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given criterion 11, when reported, then the measured recall and set size are cited.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1, when run, then it exits 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: nothing incomplete is merely listed; every open item has a GitHub Issue URL.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">README status is Complete and current-task.md is reset.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>CLAUDE.md section 7 project-close test diet gate. spec.md section 7 success criteria.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
